{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Fresh field evidence (2026-08-20) — severity looks understated\n\nObserved today while driving ~5 concurrent agents against this store:\n\n- `rebar` READS stayed fast: `rebar show <alias>` returned in ~2.9s, exit 0, throughout.\n- `rebar` WRITES (`set-file-impact`, `link`) exceeded a **600s** client timeout — 200x+ the\n  read cost on the same store at the same moment. The writes had in fact LANDED; only the\n  response was outstanding, so the store stayed consistent.\n\nThis is consistent with — but does NOT by itself prove — the linear drain-gate walk described\nabove. The measured figure in this ticket is 600-740 ms warm at 4,710 ticket dirs on an idle\nmachine. What today adds is the interaction term: the gate's cost is a full store walk, so it\nis a function of BOTH store size AND machine load. Under CPU contention (load avg 12, several\nCPU-bound processes) a 600 ms linear scan does not degrade linearly — it queues behind every\nother runnable process, and the write path wears the whole delay.\n\nWhat would actually prove it: time `Q.pending_enrichment` directly under induced CPU load and\ncompare against the idle 740 ms baseline already recorded here. I did not do that, so treat\nthis as a severity signal, not a second root cause.\n\n**Suggested reconsideration of priority.** This is filed P2. Its observable effect today was\nthat ordinary tracker writes became indistinguishable from hangs, which caused me to\nmis-attribute the slowness to an unrelated worktree and nearly re-file work that had already\nsucceeded. A write path that no-ops in the common case but costs a full store walk is a\ncorrectness-of-operations problem once the store is this large, not just a latency nit.\n\nNo description edit — evidence in comments to keep any attestation current."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787250747338158001,"uuid":"24022574-aa28-4d59-bc5b-a0b94c0bbe00"}